<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Chopin returns after nineteen days of treatment, all observed by video. The night sweats stopped in the second week, he has had no fever for ten days and no blood in his sputum for twelve, and his cough is now occasional. He had mild nausea in the first week, eased by taking the tablets in the middle of breakfast, and his urine and tears are orange as expected. He has no tendon pain, tingling, yellowing, dark urine, or rash. The three sputum smears collected in the third week were all negative, and the health department released him from isolation two days ago; he will start teaching in his studio again this week, beginning with eight lessons. The baseline cultures are growing Mycobacterium tuberculosis complex, and the molecular tests show no mutations for isoniazid or fluoroquinolone resistance. He has seen the dietitian twice and drinks two supplements a day in the afternoon and evening. His mood is better now that he can see his students. The sweat chloride test was done this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Treatment</td><td>Nineteen of nineteen doses observed</td></tr><tr><td>Infection control</td><td>Three negative smears; released from isolation; teaching again this week</td></tr><tr><td>Microbiology</td><td>Cultures growing M. tuberculosis complex; no isoniazid or fluoroquinolone resistance mutations</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>49.6 kg, up 1.1 kg</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

